<h1>Jordan Villas</h1>
<p>Illinois Senate, 12th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Working Class Party. Declared write-in.</p>
<p>These names are not printed on the ballot. To vote for one, write the name in the blank write-in space for that office and fill in the oval (on a touchscreen, follow the write-in steps on screen). Votes count only for write-ins who filed a declaration. The Chicago Board of Elections does not post those names, so this list comes from the Cook County Clerk&#39;s list and campaign announcements; election judges at your polling place have the official one.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Declared write-in candidate; the name is not printed on the ballot. Says working people need a party of their own, independent of both major parties, and points to wages that lag prices, worsening working conditions, cuts to public schools and services, and immigration enforcement raids. He was removed from the ballot after a petition objection invalidated more than 1,400 of his signatures.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>FedEx delivery driver.</p>
